+# Aegis Carbon Awareness Integration
+
+This patch provides:
+- CodeCarbon wrapper for training/inference (ops/carbon/codecarbon_wrapper.py)
+- GPU power exporter using NVML (ops/monitoring/gpu_power_exporter.py)
+- Prometheus recording rules for carbon accounting (ops/monitoring/prometheus/carbon_prometheus_rules.yaml)
+- Grafana dashboard JSON (docs/carbon/grafana_dashboard.json)
+- Carbon-aware runner to delay batch jobs until low-grid-carbon windows (ops/scheduler/carbon_aware_runner.py)
+- CronJob example to schedule carbon-aware batch jobs (k8s/scheduler/carbon-aware-cronjob.yaml)
+
+Quick start:
+1. Install dependencies in a virtualenv or your container:
+   pip install -r ops/carbon/requirements.txt
+
+2. Deploy GPU power exporter on GPU nodes (DaemonSet recommended):
+   python3 ops/monitoring/gpu_power_exporter.py --port 9450
+
+3. Scrape exporter endpoint from Prometheus and import `carbon_prometheus_rules.yaml` into Prometheus.
+
+4. Start training with carbon tracking:
+   python3 ops/carbon/codecarbon_wrapper.py --entrypoint "python train.py" --project myproj --run-name r1 --mlflow-uri http://mlflow:5000
+
+5. For batch jobs, use the carbon-aware runner as an Argo/cron job entrypoint so runs occur in low-carbon windows:
+   Use k8s/scheduler/carbon-aware-cronjob.yaml as an example.
+
+Notes & caveats:
+- ElectricityMap / Carbon Aware API keys are required for real-time grid intensity. You can set ELECTRICITYMAP_API_KEY or configure CARBON_AWARE_URL to a local adapter.
+- For accurate energy accounting, prefer direct power telemetry (NVML/DCGM). CodeCarbon provides estimates when direct telemetry is unavailable.
+- Integrate MLflow to store per-run energy/CO2 metrics and visualize in Grafana.
+
